.TH QUAKESTRIKEPH-TOOLKIT 8 "18 November 2026" "QuakeStrikePH" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
quakestrikeph-toolkit \- administer the QuakeStrikePH Option 1C demo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-install.sh
\-\-archive FILE \-\-config FILE [\-\-directory PATH]
.PP
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-accounts.sh
[\-\-directory PATH]
.PP
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-config.sh
[\-\-output FILE] [\-\-directory PATH]
.PP
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-seed.sh
[\-\-directory PATH]
.PP
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-uninstall.sh
[\-\-directory PATH] [\-\-confirm]
.PP
.B sudo bash quakestrikeph-rebuild.sh
\-\-archive FILE [\-\-config FILE] [\-\-directory PATH]
.PP
Each script also accepts
.B \-\-help
without root privileges or other arguments.
.SH DESCRIPTION
These six Bash scripts prepare, install, seed, remove, and rebuild the
group's real QuakeStrikePH application for IT 123 Option 1C.
They use sanitized historical test data, PostgreSQL, Redis, Docker Compose,
and the reviewed SEIS 1.0.1 model.
Run administrative operations as root on the group's dedicated Linux server.
Installation supports Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Debian 13 with systemd;
course approval and execution testing are separate from distribution support.
.PP
Before an offline deployment, prepare the distribution's cached APT packages
and the trusted application archive as described in TESTING.md.
The archive must include source files, model artifacts,
images.tar, and prediction-image.tar at its root.
Keep credentials and existing bootstrap evidence out of the archive.
.PP
The default installation directory is /srv/quakestrikeph.
For a different deployment directory, use a dedicated direct child of /srv.
The fixed Compose project is quakestrikeph-sam:
changing the directory does not create an independent Docker deployment.
Keep the toolkit outside the installation directory.
.PP
The deployment order is accounts, configuration, installation, accounts again,
then seed. The second accounts pass applies final file permissions.
The rebuild script coordinates this order and checks web responses afterward.
Use the same prepared release and matching credentials for repeated runs.
Installation briefly stops application services; failed stages are not rolled back.
.PP
Compose uses the native local Docker socket and an explicit environment.
Put application settings in the private configuration file;
exported shell passwords and URLs cannot override it.
The local website is http://127.0.0.1:4321.
Map tiles and optional sign-in features may require internet access.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-install.sh
Requires \-\-archive FILE (prepared .tar.gz) and \-\-config FILE
(private environment file with mode 600 or 400).
The optional \-\-directory PATH selects the installation directory.
Rejects unsafe or unrelated destinations and conflicting installed credentials.
Installs Docker from cached packages, loads images, deploys files,
initializes the database/schema/model, and verifies Backend and Bulletin HTTP
responses. Keeps existing database volumes. Run accounts again and then seed
to finish the demo setup.
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-accounts.sh
Accepts \-\-directory PATH.
Creates or reuses the locked quakestrikeph user/group with UID/GID 10001,
without a login shell or sudo/Docker group access.
Sets code directories and shell scripts to 750 and ordinary files to 640,
owned by root:quakestrikeph.
Keeps the installed .env root-owned with mode 600.
Bootstrap evidence is service-owned, with directories 700 and files 600.
Refuses conflicting identities, unsafe paths, links, and mounted targets.
Does not change Docker-managed database volume ownership.
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-config.sh
Accepts \-\-output FILE (default /root/demo.env) and \-\-directory PATH.
Validates an existing output without replacing it; if both configuration
copies exist, they must match.
If output is missing, reuses a valid installed .env.
For a new setup, generates four distinct passwords and matching local URLs.
New files are root-owned with mode 600; existing files may use 600 or 400.
The output parent must already exist, be root-owned, and not be writable
by group or others. Keep it outside Git and the installation directory.
This is a generator for the reviewed demo, not a password-rotation tool.
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-seed.sh
Accepts \-\-directory PATH and requires a completed installation.
Checks the packaged fixture's SHA-256, imports it through the application,
checks readiness, and starts Dispatcher and Prediction Worker.
Waits up to five minutes for a successful saved forecast.
A fresh import stores four earthquake records; repeated runs reuse records
and bootstrap evidence. Four rejected fixture rows are expected.
This seeds test data; it does not restore arbitrary backups or enable live ingestion.
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-uninstall.sh
Accepts \-\-directory PATH. Without \-\-confirm, validates and previews
removal without deleting anything.
.B Adding \-\-confirm permanently deletes the deployment's data.
Checks the project labels, container directory, expected data volumes,
and service identity before removing project containers, associated anonymous
storage, named data volumes, networks, installed files, and the service account/group.
Keeps Docker packages, cached images, and preparation files outside the target.
Already-absent resources are accepted, but local Docker must still respond.
If removal fails, inspect the error before retrying; earlier removals are not undone.
.TP
.B quakestrikeph-rebuild.sh
Requires \-\-archive FILE. Accepts \-\-config FILE (default /root/demo.env)
and \-\-directory PATH. Keep the other deployment scripts beside it.
Checks inputs and reports disk space with df for /tmp, /srv, and /var/lib;
the report is not a guarantee of sufficient capacity.
Runs the deployment sequence, waits for the seed's saved forecast,
then checks Backend and Bulletin HTTP responses inside their containers.
Stops on the first failure. Never calls uninstall or resets database volumes.
Use a separate disposable server for a fresh rebuild test.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run these commands from the toolkit directory in Bash.
Prepare inputs using TESTING.md first; these are real deployment commands.
.PP
Run the individual deployment stages in order:
.nf
sudo bash quakestrikeph-accounts.sh
sudo bash quakestrikeph-config.sh \-\-output /root/demo.env
sudo bash quakestrikeph-install.sh \e
    \-\-archive /root/quakestrikeph-with-prediction.tar.gz \e
    \-\-config /root/demo.env
sudo bash quakestrikeph-accounts.sh
sudo bash quakestrikeph-seed.sh
.fi
.PP
Alternatively, use the coordinator on the prepared disposable server:
.nf
sudo bash quakestrikeph-rebuild.sh \e
    \-\-archive /root/quakestrikeph-with-prediction.tar.gz
.fi
.PP
Preview uninstall only:
.nf
sudo bash quakestrikeph-uninstall.sh \-\-directory /srv/quakestrikeph
.fi
.PP
Do not add \-\-confirm on the working demo.
Actual uninstall and an already-removed repeat run passed on the separate
QuakeStrikePH-Rehearsal deployment. The working demo was not uninstalled.
The subsequent real rebuild recreated its database and saved forecast using the
preserved external credentials. Docker and cached images were retained as designed.
The separate WSL testing environment completed the real rebuild after correcting its
runtime network/mount setup, without deleting volumes or changing credentials.
A complete repeat run also preserved the records, forecast ID, and credentials.
See TESTING.md for the isolated testing network and host ports 14321/13000.
An uninterrupted first attempt on another fresh import remains unverified.
.PP
Read help or this manual without running a deployment:
.nf
bash quakestrikeph-rebuild.sh \-\-help
man ./man/quakestrikeph-toolkit.8
.fi
.SH FILES
Paths below use the defaults; \-\-directory and configuration options
change the corresponding locations.
.TP
.B README.md
Bundle preparation, configuration requirements, verification records,
and current testing limits.
.TP
.B /root/demo.env
Private external demo configuration. Preserve it for repeated installations.
.TP
.B /srv/quakestrikeph/.env
Installed root-only configuration. Never commit it or print its credentials.
.TP
.B /srv/quakestrikeph/infrastructure/compose.checkoff.yml
Installer-generated override used with the application's Compose files.
.TP
.B /srv/quakestrikeph/bootstrap-snapshots/
Private bootstrap evidence, including bootstrap-readiness.json.
Keep it with its corresponding database; do not copy it into a fresh release.
.TP
.B /var/cache/apt/archives/
Cached distribution packages for offline installation.
.TP
.B /var/run/docker.sock
Native local Docker Engine socket.
.TP
.B Docker data and logs
The named volumes are quakestrikeph-sam_postgres_data and
quakestrikeph-sam_redis_data. Do not edit their host files directly.
Scripts print diagnostics to the terminal; they do not create automatic
log files or backups. Application logs are managed by Docker; for example,
use docker logs quakestrikeph-sam-prediction-worker-1.
Keep separately prepared archives and backups outside Git and the installation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Requested operation completed, help displayed, or uninstall preview completed.
For rebuild, seed verification and both final HTTP checks passed.
.TP
.B 1
A reported validation or operation failure. Read the diagnostic and correct
the problem before retrying. Changes already made are not rolled back.
.PP
Any nonzero status is failure; a shell startup error or interruption may
produce another nonzero status. No additional toolkit-specific codes are defined.
